        "original_id": "4e24cc14-4296-5ce6-a440-503398a0aac2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Užupis, Freetown Christiania, Belmontas, Rasos, Vilnia River, Paris, Copenhagen\n- Concepts: bohemic atmosphere, laissez-faire atmosphere, artist communities, public closure and reopening\n\nFacts:\n- Užupis has been popular with artists for some time.\n- Užupis has been compared to Montmartre in Paris because of its bohemic and laissez-faire atmosphere.\n- Užupis has also been compared to Freetown Christiania in Copenhagen because of its bohemic and laissez-faire atmosphere.\n- In April 2011, residents of Freetown Christiania temporarily closed it to the public while discussions with the Danish government about its future continued.\n- After the temporary closure in April 2011, Freetown Christiania reopened to the public.\n- Belmontas is located in the Rasos area on the right bank of the Vilnia River, east of Užupis.",
